      "has_audio_listener_component": true,
      "audio_listener_component": {},
      "has_script_component": true,
      "script_component": {
       "script_components": [
        {
         "type": "GalleryTour",
         "@slot": "fedbb409-4d71-ae40-91ba-d6d91c9cda59",
         "stops": "1.60 1.70 0.40 6.0 -26.0|Physically Based|Base color, metallic and roughness: one Standard graph, its values per instance. Metals take their color from measured reflectance. Dielectrics reflect four percent at normal incidence.\n0.00 1.75 9.40 10.0 0.0|Scanned Surfaces|Photographed texture sets: color, normal, and occlusion, roughness and metallic packed in one map. A graph per set, tiling and tint exposed as parameters.\n0.00 1.80 18.60 5.0 0.0|Depth From Height|Parallax Occlusion steps through a height map along the view, so stones hide what lies behind them. Facing each: the same maps as a normal map alone.\n0.00 1.75 27.40 10.0 0.0|Procedural|No textures: noise, Voronoi cells, waves and Color Ramps make every surface here, at any resolution.\n0.00 1.75 36.40 10.0 0.0|Stylized and Effects|Emissive, see-through and cut-out looks from the same graph: additive glows, glass that bends what is behind it, clear or frosted, dissolving edges, toon bands, a cubemap mirror.\n0.00 2.30 45.20 18.0 0.0|Motion|World Position Offset moves vertices in the material: wind around each plant's own pivot, a banner's waves, see-through water, a twist. Shadows and motion vectors follow.\n0.00 2.70 54.00 20.0 0.0|Layers|Material Attributes blend whole surfaces: rock, grass, mud and snow by slope and height, moss on the faces looking up, puddles in the hollows.\n0.00 2.00 62.40 11.0 0.0|Imported Assets|glTF models with their own PBR maps, imported as Standard graph materials: leather, brass, glazed ceramic, glass.\n0.00 2.40 70.80 14.0 0.0|Decals and Post Process|Decal materials lay color, normals and roughness onto whatever is in their box: puddles, markings, damage. A Post Process material draws over the view: here it outlines the exhibits marked by a Post Process Mask.\n0.00 1.85 82.20 6.0 0.0|Blood and Gore|Drag across the dummy to slash it, or click to stab. GoreDummy.cs throws every drop of blood and lays a Decal material where it lands; cuts, stumps and pools are decals too. Deep cuts cut off limbs or spill guts, prefabs with physics.",
         "glideSeconds": 2.5999999046325685,
         "dwellSeconds": 9.0,
         "autoTour": false,
         "flySpeed": 3.0,
         "lookSensitivity": 10.0,
         "hudEntity": "HUD"
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    }
   ]
